{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ומבמות הגיא", :translit "u-me-bamot ha-gay", :gloss "and from the high places of the valley"} {:he "בא מות בגי", :translit "ba mot ba-gay", :gloss "death came in the valley"} {:he "ויקבור אותו בגיא", :translit "vi-kavor oto ba-gay", :gloss "and He buried him in the valley"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Rearrangement of the letters of מבמות הגיא yields בא מות בגי, reading 'death came in the valley'"}], :frame {:text "Deuteronomy 34:6 states that God buried Moses in the valley (ויקבור אותו בגיא). The Ba'al HaTurim links the phrase 'from Bamoth of the valley' in Numbers 21:20 to Moses' death by rearranging its letters to spell 'death came in the valley,' connecting the Israelites' journey through this location to the death and burial of Moses described in Deuteronomy 34:6.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 34:6" "Numbers 21:20"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Rearrangement of the letters of מבמות הגיא yields בא מות בגי, reading 'death came in the valley'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:29.675634350Z", :model "glm-5.2"}